Create one high-fidelity visual concept for the Urkaaaz Android Ad Reward
screen. This is a screen-design study only. Do not edit production code,
implement ads, or generate a production background or runtime asset.

## Reference inputs

- The user will attach screenshots of the current Shop, Dashboard, and Loadout
  screens. Treat all three as equal references for the shared Urkaaaz visual
  language: painterly fantasy scenery, dark translucent panels, carved
  wood/iron details, restrained warm-gold trim, pale readable text, and
  consistent framed buttons.
- Use the Dashboard screenshot to understand where the `AD REWARD` entry
  belongs in the app, but do not copy the Dashboard layout or its profile
  summary.
- Use the Shop and Loadout screenshots for shared panel, button, typography,
  icon, and ornament treatment only. Do not copy their screen layouts or
  content.
- The planned Ad Reward is an optional additional Life for watching an ad.
  The feature is not active without a configured ad provider. This image is a
  visual proposal and must not imply that ads or the reward currently work in
  the app.
- Do not assume any additional reward rules, limits, availability conditions,
  ad provider, or account state beyond that description.

## Output

- Generate exactly one PNG: `ad_reward_screen_concept_01.png`.
- Save it under `assets_src/ad-reward/screen-concepts/`.
- Canvas: exactly 1920 × 1080 pixels, landscape 16:9.
- Show the complete Android screen edge-to-edge. No phone frame, device
  mockup, presentation board, annotations, alternate screens, watermark, or
  signature.
- This is a visual concept for review. Keep scenery, panels, controls, icon,
  and text visually separable so the screen can be rebuilt with native
  Android views and individual assets. Do not flatten the interface into one
  production background.

## Screen content and hierarchy

- Design a dedicated Ad Reward offer screen reached from the Dashboard.
  Include a clear `BACK` control at the upper-left and a prominent `AD REWARD`
  heading. Back returns to the preceding screen; do not add routes to Shop,
  Loadout, Campaign, or a match.
- Make the offer immediately understandable: watching an ad is proposed to
  grant an additional Life. Give the reward a single focal treatment with a
  life/heart emblem and the short label `EXTRA LIFE`.
- Show one prominent primary action labeled `WATCH AD`. It is a proposed
  visual affordance only, not a claim that the action is wired or available.
- Keep any explanatory copy extremely short and legible. Do not invent a
  video duration, reward quantity, cooldown, daily cap, eligibility rule,
  current Life count, or guarantee that an ad is available. If a value or
  status would otherwise be needed, omit it instead of using fabricated data.
- Keep the offer calm, optional, and trustworthy rather than urgent or
  casino-like. The screen should not resemble a third-party ad, a video
  player, or an ad network landing page.
- Use one clear visual hierarchy: title and Back control, central reward
  offer, then one gold-emphasized `WATCH AD` button. Keep decoration
  subordinate to the reward and action.
- Do not include an OrCoins balance, player profile summary, campaign map,
  Shop tabs, Loadout selections, RESET control, language selector, event
  icons, or unrelated navigation.

## Layout direction

- Create a full-bleed, painterly fantasy atmosphere that feels native to the
  attached Urkaaaz screen references. Keep the area behind the offer calm and
  low-detail enough for strong text contrast; do not invent a new named
  location, character, or story event.
- Use a centered, generously spaced offer panel, or a composition with
  similarly clear focus if the attached screenshots establish a stronger
  shared pattern. Keep all essential controls within generous screen-edge
  safe margins.
- Use a dark charcoal/iron panel with restrained bronze or warm-gold edging,
  subtle carved details, and pale text. Reserve the brightest gold for the
  reward emblem and primary action rather than every border or element.
- Render the life emblem as a clear, single reward symbol. Match the shape,
  color language, and level of detail of the life/heart icon visible in the
  attached Dashboard screenshot when it is legible; do not substitute a
  different reward such as gold, a spell, an avatar, or an item.
- Use the game's Cinzel SemiBold-style typography for the heading and
  prominent labels, with compact high-contrast supporting text.
- Keep button text, reward label, and any supporting copy visually separate
  from scenery and suitable for live UI. Do not bake variable data or
  changeable UI text into the background.

## Shared component treatment

- Match the shared Shop, Dashboard, and Loadout appearance: painterly
  atmosphere, charcoal/dark-iron panels, carved wood accents, restrained
  bronze/gold edging, and pale high-contrast typography.
- Follow their actual button and frame proportions, corner treatments, border
  thickness, button depth, typography, and level of ornament. Do not
  introduce a competing interface style.
- Reuse visual motifs or approved components apparent in the attached
  screenshots when available to the generation tool. If the screenshots do
  not provide a usable exact asset, keep the concept separable and visually
  compatible; do not claim to reproduce an unseen production asset.
- Keep the background and every foreground UI layer distinct. Do not use any
  attached screenshot as a flattened screen background.

## Negative requirements

- No claim that an ad provider, rewarded-video flow, or Life grant is
  implemented or currently available.
- No invented reward quantity, timer, cooldown, daily limit, eligibility,
  availability state, current Life count, or profile data.
- No provider logos, fake ad footage, video-player controls, countdown,
  progress bar, subscription, payment, social, login, or account controls.
- No OrCoins, Shop offer grid, Loadout carousel, campaign map, battle HUD,
  RESET control, language selector, or event feed.
- No additional rewards, mechanics, screens, or navigation routes.
- No copied Shop, Dashboard, or Loadout composition; use those screenshots
  only as references for the shared visual system.
- No illegible pseudo-text, excessive ornament, urgent flashing treatment,
  device bezel, watermark, or signature.

## Review checklist

- Confirm the result is one complete 1920 × 1080 landscape screen concept with
  no device frame.
- Confirm Shop, Dashboard, and Loadout references informed a consistent
  shared Urkaaaz visual style without copying their screen layouts.
- Confirm the screen clearly presents the proposed additional-Life reward and
  has one visually dominant `WATCH AD` action.
- Confirm the reward and action are presented as a design concept only, with
  no invented quantity, rules, availability, balance, or ad provider.
- Confirm scenery, offer panel, icon, controls, and text remain visually
  separable and suitable for native UI recreation.
- Do not import the result as a single runtime screen background.
